225 828 1909 (CP/M 3 manages and supervises your computer's resources, including memory and disk storage,) 1909 SB
225 887 1763 (the console \(screen and keyboard\), printer, and communications devices. It also manages) 1763 SB
225 946 1876 (information stored magnetically on disks by grouping this information into files of programs or) 1876 SB
225 1005 1871 (data.  CP/M 3 can copy files from a disk to your computer's memory, or to a peripheral device) 1871 SB
225 1064 1883 (such as a printer, To do this, CP/M 3 places various programs in memory and executes them in) 1883 SB
225 1124 984 (response to commands you enter at your console.) 984 SB
225 1183 13 ( ) 13 SB
225 1242 1793 (Once in memory, a program executes through a set of steps that instruct your computer to) 1793 SB
225 1301 1871 (perform a certain task.  You can use CP/M 3 to create your own programs, or you can choose) 1871 SB
225 1360 1901 (from the wide variety of CP/M 3 application programs that entertain you, educate you, and help) 1901 SB
225 1419 912 (you solve commercial and scientific problems.) 912 SB
