225 1656 1924 (Digital Research provides two kinds of CP/M 3 systems: banked and nonbanked. Your computer) 1924 SB
225 1715 1923 (dealer can tell you if you have a banked or nonbanked system.  The banked system requires more) 1923 SB
225 1774 1921 (memory, but in turn provides more memory space for application programs.  The banked version) 1921 SB
225 1834 1168 (also has additional enhancements that are noted in the text.) 1168 SB
225 1952 1950 (The minimum hardware requirement for both versions of CP/M 3 is a computer based on an 8080,) 1950 SB
225 2011 1873 (8085, or equivalent microprocessor, a console device \(generally a keyboard and display device) 1873 SB
225 2070 1903 (such as a CRT screen\), and at least one floppy disk drive.  To use all the capabilities of CP/M 3,) 1903 SB
225 2129 1868 (you should have two disk drives.  At least one should be a single density floppy drive, because) 1868 SB
225 2189 1638 (CP/M 3 and most CP/M applications are distributed on single density floppy disks.) 1638 SB
