290 775 570 (   1.1 How to Start CP/M 3) 570 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
225 895 1699 (          Starting or loading CP/M 3 means reading a copy of the operating system from) 1699 SB
225 954 1704 (        your CP/M 3 system disk \(1 of 2 of your distribution disks\) into your computer's) 1704 SB
225 1013 279 (        memory,) 279 SB
225 1131 1692 (          First, check that your computer's power is on.  Next, insert the CP/M 3 system) 1692 SB
225 1190 1748 (        disk into your initial drive.  In this section, assume that the initial drive is A and the) 1748 SB
225 1250 1848 (        disk is removable.  Close the drive door.  Then, press the RESET or RESTART button.) 1848 SB
225 1309 1756 (        This automatically loads CP/M 3 into memory.  This process is called booting, cold) 1756 SB
225 1368 716 (        starting, or loading the system.) 716 SB
225 1486 1688 (          After CP/M 3 is loaded into memory, a message similar to the following is dis-) 1688 SB
225 1545 553 (        played on your screen:) 553 SB
225 1664 723 (            CP/M 3            Version V.V) 723 SB
225 1782 1782 (        The version number, represented above by V.V, tells you the version of CP/M 3 that) 1782 SB
225 1841 1743 (        you own.  After this display, the following two-character message appears on your) 1743 SB
225 1900 244 (        screen:) 244 SB

%%BeginResource: font MSTT31c363
/G3e [28.0 0.0 1.0 5.0 27.0 30.0]
/G3e {
    26 25 true [1 0 0 -1 -1.0 30.0] {<80000000e0000000780000001f00000007c0000000f00000003c0000000f00000003c0000000f800
00003e0000000780000001c00000078000003e000000f8000003c000000f0000003c000000f00000
07c000001f00000078000000e000000080000000>} imagemask 
  }
  62 /G3e MSTT31c363 AddChar
%%EndResource

225 2019 180 (        A >) 180 SB
225 2137 1715 (          This is the CP/M 3 system prompt.  The system prompt tells you that CP/M 3 is) 1715 SB
225 2196 1786 (        ready to read a command from your keyboard.  In this example, the prompt also tells) 1786 SB
225 2255 1739 (        you that drive A is your default drive.  This means that until you tell CP/M 3 to do) 1739 SB
225 2315 1769 (        otherwise, it looks for program and data files on the disk in drive A. It also tells you) 1769 SB
225 2374 1654 (        that you are logged in as user 0, by the absence of a user number other than 0.) 1654 SB
1166 2906 67 (1-1) 67 SB
