0 0 0 fC
225 152 558 (    1.2 The Command Line) 558 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
225 270 1629 (       CP/M 3 performs tasks according to specific commands that you type at your) 1629 SB
225 330 1757 (    keyboard.  A CP/M 3 command line is composed of a command keyword, an optional) 1757 SB
225 389 1698 (    command tail, and a carriage return keystroke.  The command keyword identifies a) 1698 SB
225 448 1695 (    command \(program\) to be executed.  The command tail can contain extra informa-) 1695 SB
225 507 1707 (    tion for the command, such as a filename or parameters.  To end the command line,) 1707 SB
225 566 1709 (    you must press the carriage return or ENTER key.  The following example shows a) 1709 SB
225 625 341 (    command line.) 341 SB
225 744 399 (    A>DIR MYFILE) 399 SB
225 862 1659 (    The characters that the user types are slanted to distinguish them from characters) 1659 SB
225 921 1765 (    that the system displays.  In this example, DIR is the command keyword and MYFILE) 1765 SB
225 980 1726 (    is the command tail.  The carriage return keystroke does not appear on the screen or) 1726 SB
225 1040 1608 (    in the example.  You must remember to press the carriage return key to send a) 1608 SB
225 1099 1676 (    command line to CP/M 3 for processing.  Note that the carriage return key can be) 1676 SB
225 1158 1663 (    marked ENTER, RETURN,, CR, or something similar on your keyboard.  In this) 1663 SB
225 1217 1035 (    guide, RETURN signifies the carriage return key.) 1035 SB
225 1335 1714 (       As you type characters at  the keyboard, they   appear on your screen. The single-) 1714 SB
225 1395 1691 (    character position indicator, called the cursor, moves to the right as you type char-) 1691 SB
225 1454 1705 (    acters.  If you make a typing error, press either the BACKSPACE key \(if your key-) 1705 SB
225 1513 1626 (    board has one\) or CTRL-H to move the cursor to the left and correct the error.) 1626 SB
225 1572 1641 (    CTRL is the abbreviation for the Control key.  To type a control character, hold) 1641 SB
225 1631 1685 (    down the Control key and press the required letter key.  For example, to move the) 1685 SB
225 1690 1178 (    cursor to the left, hold down CTRL and press the H key.) 1178 SB
225 1809 1744 (       You can type the keyword and command tail in any        combination of upper-case) 1744 SB
225 1868 1707 (    and lower-case letters.  CP/M 3 treats all letters in the command line as upper-case.) 1707 SB
225 1986 1683 (       Generally, you type a command line directly after the system prompt.  However,) 1683 SB
225 2045 1551 (    CP/M 3 does allow spaces between the prompt and the command keyword.) 1551 SB
1166 2933 67 (1-2) 67 SB
