225 152 1778 (      CP/M 3 recognizes only correctly spelled command keywords.       If you make a typ-) 1778 SB
225 211 1665 (    ing error and press RETURN before correcting your mistake, CP/M 3 echoes the) 1665 SB
225 270 1715 (    command line followed with a question mark.  If you mistype the DIR command, as) 1715 SB
225 330 913 (    in the following example, CP/M 3 responds) 913 SB
225 448 203 (    A>DJR) 203 SB
225 507 161 (    DJR?) 161 SB
225 625 1756 (    to tell you that it cannot find the command keyword.  To correct simple typing errors,) 1756 SB
225 685 1667 (    use the BACKSPACE key, or hold down the CTRL key and press H to move the) 1667 SB
225 744 1729 (    cursor to the left.  CP/M 3 supports other control characters that help you efficiently) 1729 SB
225 803 1702 (    edit command lines.  Section 3 tells how to use control characters to edit command) 1702 SB
225 862 1116 (    lines and other information you enter at your console.) 1116 SB
