225 152 1753 (         Data processing professionals avoid losing programs and data by making copies of) 1753 SB
225 211 1739 (      valuable files.  Always make a working copy of any new program that you purchase) 1739 SB
225 270 1725 (      and save the original.  If the program is accidentally erased from the working copy,) 1725 SB
225 330 905 (      you can easily restore it from the original.) 905 SB
225 448 1614 (         It is also wise to make frequent copies of new programs or data files as you) 1614 SB
225 507 1777 (       develop them.  The frequency of making copies varies with each programmer.  How-) 1777 SB
225 566 1723 (       ever, as a general rule, make a copy at the point where it takes ten to twenty times) 1723 SB
225 625 1363 (       longer to reenter the information than it takes to make the copy.) 1363 SB
225 744 1749 (         So far, we have not discussed any commands that change information recorded on) 1749 SB
225 803 1705 (       your CP/M 3 system disk.  Before we do, make a few working copies of the your) 1705 SB
225 862 443 (       distribution disks.) 443 SB
225 981 65 (     ) 65 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c370 font
290 980 1033 (  1.4 How to Make Copies of Your CP/M 3 Disks) 1033 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
225 1100 1717 (         To back up your CP/M 3 disks, you need two or more floppy disks for the back-) 1717 SB
225 1159 1682 (       ups.  The back-up disks can be new or used.  You might want to format new, or) 1682 SB
225 1218 1752 (       reformat used disks with the disk formatting program that accompanies your partic-) 1752 SB
225 1277 1785 (       ular computer.  If the disks are used, be sure that there are no other files on the disks.) 1785 SB
225 1396 1678 (         If your computer's manufacturer has provided a special program to copy disks,) 1678 SB
225 1455 1693 (       you might use it to make back-ups of your distribution disks.  Otherwise, use the) 1693 SB
225 1514 1743 (       COPYSYS and PIP utility programs found on your CP/M 3 distribution disks.  PIP) 1743 SB
225 1573 1674 (       can copy all program and data files, but only COPYSYS can copy the operating) 1674 SB
225 1632 1709 (       system.  Note that the COPYSYS utility distributed by Digital Resarch only func-) 1709 SB
225 1691 1770 (       tions with eight-inch, single-density drives.  However, your computer's manufacturer) 1770 SB
225 1751 1342 (       might have modified COPYSYS to work with your equipment.) 1342 SB
225 1869 1703 (         This section shows how to make distribution disk back-ups on a system that has) 1703 SB
225 1928 1768 (       two drives: drive A and drive B. Your drives might be named with other letters from) 1768 SB
225 1987 1701 (       the range A through P. To make a copy of your CP/M 3 distribution system disk,) 1701 SB
225 2046 1718 (       labeled 1 of 2, first use the COPYSYS utility to copy the operating system loader.) 1718 SB
225 2106 1748 (       Make sure that your distribution system disk is in drive A, the default drive, and the) 1748 SB
225 2165 1709 (       blank disk is in drive B. Then enter the following command at the system prompt:) 1709 SB
225 2283 392 (       A >COPYSYS) 392 SB
1166 2934 67 (1-5) 67 SB
