225 1868 1729 (    This PIP command copies all the files in your disk directory to drive B from drive A.) 1729 SB
225 1927 1752 (    PIP displavs the message COPYING followed by each filename as the copy operation) 1752 SB
225 1986 1534 (    proceeds. When PIP finishes copying, CP/M 3 displays the system prompt.) 1534 SB
225 2105 1643 (      Now you have an exact copy of the distribution disk 1 of 2 in drive B. Remove) 1643 SB
225 2164 1667 (    the original from drive A and store it in a safe place.  If your original remains safe) 1667 SB
225 2223 1610 (    and unchanged, you can easily restore your CP/M 3 program files if something) 1610 SB
225 2282 671 (    happens to your working copy.) 671 SB
