225 152 1627 (        Remove the copy from drive B and insert it in drive A. Use this copy as your) 1627 SB
225 211 1739 (      CP/M 3 system disk to make more back-ups, to try the examples shown throughout) 1739 SB
225 270 1681 (      this manual, and to start CP/M 3 the next time you turn on your computer.  Cold) 1681 SB
225 330 967 (      start the computer to check copy operations.) 967 SB
225 448 1593 (        You still need to make a back-up copy of distribution disk 2 of 2. This disk) 1593 SB
225 507 1762 (      contains programmer's utility programs and source files.  Place another new or refor-) 1762 SB
225 566 1417 (      matted disk in drive B. This time, type only the command keyword:) 1417 SB
225 685 214 (      A>PIP) 214 SB
225 803 1651 (      PIP responds with an asterisk prompt, *. You can now remove disk I of 2 from) 1651 SB
225 862 1685 (      drive A and insert the disk you want to copy, disk 2 of 2. Type the following PIP) 1685 SB
225 921 1045 (      command after the asterisk prompt, for example,) 1045 SB
225 1040 329 (      *B: =A: *. *) 329 SB
225 1158 1736 (      Again, PIP displays the message COPYING, followed by each filename.  When PIP) 1736 SB
225 1217 1746 (      completes the copy and displays the asterisk prompt, press RETURN.  CP/M 3 then) 1746 SB
225 1276 1654 (      displays the familiar A> system prompt.  You now have a copy of disk 2 of 2 in) 1654 SB
225 1335 1663 (      drive B. Remove both 2 of 2 disks and store them in a safe place.  You can now) 1663 SB
225 1395 1385 (      reinsert your working system disk and continue to use the system.) 1385 SB

