225 598 1735 (          CP/M 3's most important task is to access and maintain files on your disks.  With) 1735 SB
225 657 1781 (        CP/M 3 you can create, read, write, copy, and erase disk files.  This section tells you) 1781 SB
225 716 1692 (        what a file is, how to create, name, and access a file, and how files are stored on) 1692 SB
225 775 1567 (        your disks.  It also tells how to change disks and change the default drive.) 1567 SB
