329 2137 588 (2.2 How Are Files Created?) 588 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
225 2256 1767 (         There are many ways to create a file.  One way is to use a text editor.  The CP/M 3) 1767 SB
225 2316 1734 (        text editor ED \(described in Section 6\) can create a file and assign it the name you) 1734 SB
225 2375 1681 (        specify.  You can also create a file by copying an existing file to a new location,) 1681 SB
225 2434 1793 (        perhaps renaming it in the process.  Under CP/M 3, you can use the PIP command to) 1793 SB
225 2493 1762 (        copy and rename files.  Finally, some programs such as MAC" create output files as) 1762 SB
225 2552 571 (        they process input files.) 571 SB
1166 2907 67 (2-1) 67 SB
