303 1513 789 ( 2.4 Do You Have the Correct Drive?) 789 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
225 1632 1745 (          When you type a file specification in a command tall without a drive specifier, the) 1745 SB
225 1691 1634 (       program looks for the file in the drive named by the system prompt, called the) 1634 SB
225 1751 1144 (       default drive.  For example, if you type the command) 1144 SB
225 1869 604 (       A>DIR COPYSYS.COM) 604 SB
225 1987 1730 (       DIR looks in the directory of the disk in drive A for COPYSYS.COM. If you have) 1730 SB
225 2046 1704 (       another drive, B for example, you need a way to tell CP/M 3 to access the disk in) 1704 SB
225 2106 1705 (       drive B instead.  For this reason, CP/M 3 lets you precede a filename with a drive) 1705 SB
225 2165 1126 (       specifier.  For example, in response to the command) 1126 SB
225 2283 578 (       A>DIR B:MYFILE.LIB) 578 SB
