225 152 1644 (       The two wildcard characters are ?, which matches any single letter in the same) 1644 SB
225 211 1708 (     position, and *, which matches any character at that position and any other charac-) 1708 SB
225 270 1680 (     ters remaining in the filename or filetype.  The following list presents the rules for) 1680 SB
225 330 386 (     using wildcards.) 386 SB
225 448 1492 (          o   A ? matches any character in a name, including a space character.) 1492 SB
225 507 1691 (          o   An * must be the last, or only, character in the filename or filetype. CP/M 3) 1691 SB
225 566 1573 (               internally replaces an * with ? characters to the end of the filename or) 1573 SB
225 625 367 (                filetype.) 367 SB
225 685 1678 (          o   When the filename to match is shorter than eight characters, CP/M 3 treats) 1678 SB
225 744 879 (                the name as if it ends with spaces.) 879 SB
225 803 1660 (          o   When the filetype to match is shorter than three characters, CP/M 3 treats) 1660 SB
225 862 920 (                the filetype as if it ends with spaces.) 920 SB
225 980 1572 (       Suppose, for example, you have a disk that contains the following six files:) 1572 SB
225 1099 1658 (     A. COM     AA. COM      AAA*COM        B. COM     A. ASM      and B.ASM) 1658 SB
225 1217 1550 (     The following wildcard specifications match all, or a portion of, these files:) 1550 SB
225 1335 933 (     *.*                        is treated as ????????.???) 933 SB
225 1454 838 (    ????????.???         matches all six names) 838 SB
225 1572 980 (     *.COM                 is treated as ????????.COM) 980 SB
225 1690 983 (     ????????.COM     matches the first four names) 983 SB
225 1809 1024 (     ?.COM                 matches A.COM and B.COM) 1024 SB
225 1927 834 (     ? . *                       is treated as ?. ? ? ?) 834 SB
225 2045 1437 (     ?*???                       matches A.COM, B.COM, A.ASM, and B.ASM) 1437 SB
225 2164 1161 (     A?.COM                      matches A.COM and AA.COM) 1161 SB
225 2282 1094 (     A*.COM                      is treated as A???????.COM) 1094 SB
225 2400 1491 (     A???????*COM                matches A.COM, AA.COM, and AAA.COM) 1491 SB
1166 2933 67 (2-6) 67 SB
225 77 1921 (2.6 Accessing Multiple Files                                                                        CP/M 3 User's Guide) 1921 SB
