225 626 1709 (          CP/M 3 records the filename, filetype, password, user number, and attributes of) 1709 SB
225 686 1727 (       each file in a special area of the disk called the directory.  In the directory, CP/M 3) 1727 SB
225 745 1213 (       also records which parts of the disk belong to which file.) 1213 SB
225 863 1759 (          CP/M 3 allocates directory and storage space for a file as records are added to the) 1759 SB
225 922 1755 (       file.  When you erase a file, CP/M 3 reclaims storage in two ways: it makes the file's) 1755 SB
225 981 1740 (       directory space available to catalog a different file, and frees the file's storage space) 1740 SB
225 1041 1776 (       for later use.  It is this dynamic allocation feature that makes CP/M 3 powerful.  You) 1776 SB
225 1100 1725 (       do not have to tell CP/M 3 how big your file will become, because it automatically) 1725 SB
225 1159 1738 (       allocates more storage for a file as needed, and releases the storage for reallocation) 1738 SB
225 1218 1690 (       when the file is erased.  Use the SHOW command to determine how much space) 1690 SB
225 1277 488 (       remains on the disk.) 488 SB
