225 1515 1724 (          CP/M 3 cannot, of course, do anything to a file unless the disk that holds the file) 1724 SB
225 1574 1721 (       is inserted into a drive and the drive is ready.  When a disk is in a drive, it is online) 1721 SB
225 1633 993 (       and CP/M 3 can access its directory and files.) 993 SB
225 1752 1706 (          At some time, you will need to take a disk out of a drive and insert another that) 1706 SB
225 1811 1765 (       contains different files.  You can replace an online disk whenever you see the system) 1765 SB
225 1870 1667 (       prompt at your console.  This is a clear indication that no program is reading or) 1667 SB
225 1929 486 (       writing to the drive.) 486 SB
225 2048 1691 (          You can also remove a disk and insert a new one when an application program) 1691 SB
225 2107 1758 (       prompts you to do so.  This can occur, for example, when the data that the program) 1758 SB
225 2166 808 (       uses does not fit on one floppy disk.) 808 SB
