225 1901 1690 (         You can also use a control command to echo console output to the printer.  To) 1690 SB
225 1961 1811 (       start printer echo, press a CTRL-P.  To stop, press CTRL-P again.  While printer echo) 1811 SB
225 2020 1650 (       is in effect, any characters that appear on your screen are listed at your printer.) 1650 SB
225 2138 1717 (         You can use printer echo with a DIR command to make a list of files stored on a) 1717 SB
225 2197 1745 (       floppy disk.  You can also use CTRL-P with CTRL-S and CTRL-Q to make a hard) 1745 SB
225 2256 1659 (       copy of part of a file.  Use a TYPE command to start a display of the file at the) 1659 SB
225 2316 1767 (       console.  When the display reaches the part you need to print, press CTRL-S to stop) 1767 SB
225 2375 1768 (       the display, CTRL-P to enable printer echo, and then CTRL-Q to resume the display) 1768 SB
225 2434 1729 (       and  start pr inting. You can use another CTRL-S, CTRL-P, CTRL-Q sequence to) 1729 SB
225 2493 542 (       terminate printer echo.) 542 SB
