225 1165 1710 (         A GET command can direct CP/M 3 or a program to read a disk file for console) 1710 SB
225 1224 1694 (       input instead of the keyboard.  If the file is to be read by CP/M 3, it must contain) 1694 SB
225 1283 1779 (       standard CP/M 3 command lines.  If the file is to be read by a utility program, it must) 1779 SB
225 1342 1707 (       contain input appropriate for that program.  A file can contain both CP/M 3 com-) 1707 SB
225 1401 1653 (       mand lines and program input if it also includes a command to start a program.) 1653 SB
225 1520 1775 (         You add or omit the SYSTEM option in the GET command line to specify whether) 1775 SB
225 1579 1688 (       CP/M 3 or a utility program is to start reading the file, as shown in the following) 1688 SB
225 1638 1761 (       sample session.  If you omit the SYSTEM option, the system prompt returns so that) 1761 SB
225 1697 1661 (        you can initiate the program that is to take input from the specified file.  If you) 1661 SB
225 1756 1780 (       include the SYSTEM option, CP/M 3 immediately takes input from the specified file.) 1780 SB
