225 271 1695 (         Most CP/M 3 computer systems have a traditional console with a keyboard and) 1695 SB
225 331 1749 (      screen display.  Many also have letter-quality printers.  If you use your computer for) 1749 SB
225 390 1680 (      unusual tasks, you might want to add a different kind of character device to your) 1680 SB
225 449 1692 (      system: a line printer, a teletype terminal, a modem, or even a joystick for playing) 1692 SB
225 508 1760 (      games.  To keep track of these physically different input and output devices, CP/M 3) 1760 SB
225 567 1746 (      associates different physical devices with logical devices.  Table 3-3 gives the names) 1746 SB
225 626 1791 (      of CP/M 3 logical devices.  It also shows the physical devices assigned to these logical) 1791 SB
225 686 902 (      devices in the distributed CP/M 3 system.) 902 SB
