225 1072 1740 (         A command keyword identifies a program that resides either in memory as part of) 1740 SB
225 1131 1729 (      CP/M 3, or on a disk as a program file.  Commands that identify programs in mem-) 1729 SB
225 1190 1704 (      ory are called built-in commands.  Commands that identify program files on a disk) 1704 SB
225 1250 815 (      are called transient utility commands.) 815 SB
225 1368 1681 (         CP/M 3 has six built-in commands and over twenty transient utility commands.) 1681 SB
225 1427 1770 (      You can add utilities to your system by purchasing various CP/M 3-compatible appli-) 1770 SB
225 1486 1691 (      cation programs.  If you are an experienced programmer, you can also write your) 1691 SB
225 1545 959 (              own utilities that operate with CP/M 3.) 959 SB
225 1665 65 (     ) 65 SB
