225 1783 1626 (         Built-in commands are part of CP/M 3 and are always available for your use) 1626 SB
225 1842 1761 (      regardless of which disk you have in which drive.  Built-in commands reside in mem-) 1761 SB
225 1901 1618 (      ory as a part of CP/M 3 and therefore execute more quickly than the transient) 1618 SB
225 1961 235 (      utilities.) 235 SB
225 2079 1755 (         Some built-in commands have options that require support from a related transient) 1755 SB
225 2138 1714 (      utility.  The related transient has the same name as the built-in and has a filetype of) 1714 SB
225 2197 1662 (      COM.  This type of transient utility is loaded only when a built-in command line) 1662 SB
225 2256 1422 (      contains options that cannot be performed by the built-in command.) 1422 SB
