225 1751 1703 (     This section describes how CP/M 3 searches for program and data files on disk.  If) 1703 SB
225 1810 1676 (   it appears that CP/M 3 cannot find a program file you specified in a command line,) 1676 SB
225 1869 1581 (   the problem might be that CP/M 3 is not looking on the drive where the file is) 1581 SB
225 1928 1725 (   stored.  Therefore, you need to understand the steps CP/M 3 follows in searching for) 1725 SB
225 1987 495 (   program and data files.) 495 SB
225 2107 39 (   ) 39 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c370 font
264 2106 508 (4.4.1 Finding Data Files) 508 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
225 2225 1671 (      As you recall, when you enter a command line, CP/M 3 passes the command tail) 1671 SB
225 2284 1697 (   to the program identified by the command keyword.  If the command tail contains a) 1697 SB
225 2343 1650 (   file specification, the program calls CP/M 3 to search for the data file.  If CP/M 3) 1650 SB
225 2403 1596 (   cannot find the data file, the program displays an error message at the console.) 1596 SB
225 2462 1762 (   Typically, this message is F i 1 e n o t f o u n d or N o F i 1 e, but the message depends) 1762 SB
225 2521 1082 (   on the program identified by the command keyword.) 1082 SB
1166 2935 67 (4-4) 67 SB
