225 152 1257 (       CP/M 3 looks for SHOW.COM in the following sequence:) 1257 SB
225 270 503 (           1.  drive D, user 2) 503 SB
225 330 503 (           2.  drive D, user 0) 503 SB
225 389 502 (           3.  drive A, user 2) 502 SB
225 448 502 (           4.  drive A, user 0) 502 SB
225 566 1744 (       You can include your default drive in your drive chain with an option in a SETDEF) 1744 SB
225 625 1697 (       command.  Any drive chain you specify with SETDEF remains in effect until you) 1697 SB
225 685 617 (       restart or reset the system.) 617 SB
225 803 1707 (         You can also use a SETDEF command to enable automatic submit in your drive) 1707 SB
225 862 1303 (       chain.  See Section 4.5 for a description of automatic submit.) 1303 SB
