316 980 741 (4.5 Executing Multiple Commands) 741 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
225 1100 1590 (         In the examples so far, CP/M 3 has executed only one command at a time.) 1590 SB
225 1159 1697 (       CP/M 3 can also execute a sequence of commands.  You can enter a sequence of) 1697 SB
225 1218 1697 (       commands at the system prompt, or you can put a frequently needed sequence of) 1697 SB
225 1277 1728 (       commands in a disk file.  Once you have stored the sequence in a disk file, you can) 1728 SB
225 1336 1518 (       execute the sequence whenever you need to with a SUBMIT command.) 1518 SB
225 1455 1714 (         To enter multiple commands at the system prompt, separate each command key-) 1714 SB
225 1514 1653 (       word and associated command tail from the next keyword with an exclamation) 1653 SB
225 1573 1751 (       point, !. When you complete the sequence, press RETURN.  CP/M 3 executes your) 1751 SB
225 1632 486 (       commands in order:) 486 SB
225 1751 848 (       3A>dirsys!dir examp*.*!show [space]) 848 SB
225 1810 750 (       NON-SYSTEM FILE\(S\) EXIST) 750 SB
225 1869 439 (       3A>dir examp*.*) 439 SB
225 1928 1780 (       A: EXAMP7        : EXAMPI    TXT : EXAMP3          EXAMP2    TXT   EXAMP4) 1780 SB
225 1987 693 (       A: EXAMP5        : EXAMPG) 693 SB
225 2046 441 (       3A>show [space]) 441 SB
225 2165 604 (       A: RW, Space:     3,344K) 604 SB
1166 2934 67 (4-7) 67 SB
