225 1250 1762 (         This section describes the parts of a file specification in a command line.  There are) 1762 SB
225 1309 1694 (       four parts in a file specification; to avoid confusion, each part has a formal name:) 1694 SB
225 1427 1689 (            o   drive specifier-the optional disk drive A, B, C, ...P that contains the file or) 1689 SB
225 1486 1674 (                group of files to which you are referring.  If a drive specifier is included in) 1674 SB
225 1545 1061 (                your command line, a colon must follow it.) 1061 SB
225 1605 1638 (            o  filename-the one- to eight-character first name of a file or group of files.) 1638 SB
225 1664 1729 (            o  filetype-the optional one- to three-character category name of a file or group) 1729 SB
225 1723 1735 (                of files.  If the filetype is present, a period must separate it from the filename.) 1735 SB
225 1782 1677 (            o  password-the optional one- to eight-character password which allows you) 1677 SB
225 1841 1692 (                to protect your files.  It follows the filetype, or the filename if no filetype is) 1692 SB
225 1900 1031 (                assigned, and is preceded by a semicolon.) 1031 SB
225 2019 1781 (          If you do not include a drive specifier, CP/M 3 automatically uses the default drive.) 1781 SB
225 2078 1727 (       If you omit the period and the filetype, CP/M 3 automatically includes a filetype of) 1727 SB
225 2137 343 (       three blanks.) 343 SB
1166 2906 67 (5-1) 67 SB
