225 152 1720 (      This general form is called a file specification.  A file specification names a particu-) 1720 SB
225 211 1578 (     lar file or group of files in the directory of the on-line disk given by the drive) 1578 SB
225 270 530 (     specifier.  For example,) 530 SB
225 389 412 (     B:MYFILE.DAT) 412 SB
225 507 1787 (     is a file specification that indicates drive B:, filename MYFILE, and filetype DAT.  File) 1787 SB
225 566 649 (     specificat'on is abbreviated to) 649 SB
225 685 279 (          filespec) 279 SB
225 803 757 (     in the command syntax statements.) 757 SB
225 921 1727 (       Some CP/M 3 commands accept wildcards in the filename and filetype parts of the) 1727 SB
225 980 631 (     command tall.  For example,) 631 SB
225 1099 307 (     B:MY*.A??) 307 SB
225 1217 1699 (     is a file specification with drive specifier B:, filename MY*, and filetype A??.  This) 1699 SB
225 1276 1446 (     ambiguous file specification might match several files in the directory.) 1446 SB
225 1395 1458 (       Put together, the parts of a file specification are represented like this:) 1458 SB
225 1513 613 (          d:filename.typ;password) 613 SB
225 1631 1749 (       In the preceding form, d: represents the optional drive specifier, filename represents) 1749 SB
225 1690 1695 (     the one- to eight-character filename, and typ represents the optional one- to three-) 1695 SB
225 1750 1672 (     character filetype.  The syntax descriptions in this section use the term filespec to) 1672 SB
225 1809 1734 (     indicate any valid combination of the elements included in the file specification.  The) 1734 SB
225 1868 1766 (     following list shows valid combinations of the elements of a CP/M 3 file specification.) 1766 SB
225 1986 361 (          o   filename) 361 SB
225 2045 437 (          o   filename.typ) 437 SB
225 2105 563 (          o   filename;password) 563 SB
225 2164 639 (          o   filename.typ;password) 639 SB
225 2223 413 (          o   d: filename) 413 SB
225 2282 476 (          o   d:filename.typ) 476 SB
225 2341 602 (          o   d:filename;password) 602 SB
225 2400 704 (          o   d: filename. typ;password) 704 SB
1166 2933 67 (5-2) 67 SB
