225 152 1675 (             o The explanation section defines the general use of the command keyword,) 1675 SB
225 211 1630 (               and points out exceptions and special cases.  The explanation sometimes) 1630 SB
225 270 1604 (               includes tables or lists of options that you can use in the command line.) 1604 SB
225 389 1646 (             o  The examples section lists a number of valid command lines that use the) 1646 SB
225 448 1723 (               command keyword.  To clarify examples of interactions between you and the) 1723 SB
225 507 1670 (               operating system, the characters that you enter are slanted.  The responses) 1670 SB
225 566 1277 (               that CP/M 3 shows on your screen are in vertical type.) 1277 SB
225 685 1709 (         The notation in the syntax lines describes the general command form using these) 1709 SB
225 744 213 (        rules:) 213 SB
225 862 1601 (             o Words in capital letters must be spelled as shown, but you can use any) 1601 SB
225 921 1069 (               combination of upper- or lower-case letters.) 1069 SB
225 1040 1671 (             o The symbolic notation d:, filename, type, ;password, and filespec have the) 1671 SB
