225 271 544 (      Syntax:       COPYSYS) 544 SB
225 390 1720 (      Explanation:  The COPYSYS command copies the CP/M 3 system from a CP/M 3) 1720 SB
225 449 1610 (                    system disk to another disk.  The disk must have the same format as) 1610 SB
225 508 1604 (                    the original system disk.  For example, if the system disk is a single-) 1604 SB
225 567 1561 (                    density disk, the disk you use to copy onto must also be in single-) 1561 SB
225 626 558 (                    density format.) 558 SB
225 745 1674 (                    The COPYSYS utility copies only the system tracks onto the new disk.) 1674 SB
225 804 1644 (                    To use the new disk as a CP/M 3 system disk, you must also copy the) 1644 SB
225 863 1754 (                    system file CPM3.SYS to the new disk. COPYSYS gives you the     option) 1754 SB
225 922 1663 (                    to copy CPM3.SYS to the new disk.  To copy other files onto the new) 1663 SB
225 981 825 (                    disk,, use the PIP command.) 825 SB
225 1100 639 (      Example:      A>COPY'SYS) 639 SB
225 1159 592 (                    Copysys Ver 3.0) 592 SB
