554 687 1309 (  The DEVICE command is a transient utility that displays current) 1309 SB
225 746 1692 (                  assignments of CP/M 3 logical devices and the names of physical devices.) 1692 SB
225 805 1571 (                  DEVICE allows you to assign logical CP/M 3 devices to peripheral) 1571 SB
225 864 1663 (                  devices attached to the computer.  The DEVICE command also sets the) 1663 SB
225 923 1572 (                  communications protocol and speed of a peripheral device, and dis-) 1572 SB
225 983 1112 (                  plays or sets the current console screen size.) 1112 SB
225 1101 1253 (                  CP/M 3 supports the following five logical devices:) 1253 SB
225 1219 406 (                  CONIN:) 406 SB
225 1278 456 (                  CONOUT:) 456 SB
225 1338 408 (                  AUXIN:) 408 SB
225 1397 458 (                  AUXOUT:) 458 SB
225 1456 337 (                  LST:) 337 SB
225 1574 1455 (                  These logical devices are also known by the following names:) 1455 SB
225 1693 962 (                  CON: \(for CONIN: and CONOUT:\)) 962 SB
225 1752 1087 (                  CONSOLE: \(for CONIN: and CONOUT:\)) 1087 SB
225 1811 799 (                  KEYBOARD \(for CONIN:\)) 799 SB
225 1870 968 (                  AUX: \(for AUXIN: and AUXOUT:\)) 968 SB
225 1929 1136 (                  AUXILIARY: \(for AUXIN: and AUXOUT:\)) 1136 SB
225 1988 664 (                  PRINTER \(for LST:\)) 664 SB
225 2107 1630 (                  The physical device names on a computer vary from system to system.) 1630 SB
225 2166 1657 (                  You can use the DEVICE command to display the names and attributes) 1657 SB
225 2225 1194 (                  of the physical devices that your system accepts.) 1194 SB
1154 2935 92 (5-14) 92 SB
225 77 1903 (The DEVICE Command                                                                            CP/M 3 User's Guide) 1903 SB
