225 330 1621 (                        XON             refers to the XON/XOFF communications protocol.) 1621 SB
225 389 1604 (                                        This protocol uses two special characters in the ASCII) 1604 SB
225 448 1563 (                                          character set called XON and XDFF.  XON signals) 1563 SB
225 507 1578 (                                          transmission on, and XOFF signals transmission off.) 1578 SB
225 566 1580 (                                        Before each character is output from the computer to) 1580 SB
225 625 1538 (                                        the peripheral device, the computer checks to see if) 1538 SB
225 685 1576 (                                        there is any incoming data from the peripheral.  If the) 1576 SB
225 744 1574 (                                        incoming character is XO,FF, the computer suspends) 1574 SB
225 803 1534 (                                        all further output until it receives an XON from the) 1534 SB
225 862 1507 (                                        device, indicating that the device is again ready to) 1507 SB
225 921 886 (                                        receive more data.) 886 SB
225 1040 1686 (                        NOXON           indicates no protocol and the computer sends data to) 1686 SB
225 1099 1616 (                                        the device whether or not the device is ready to receive) 1616 SB
225 1158 560 (                                        it.) 560 SB
225 1276 1576 (                        baud-rate       is the speed of the device. The system accepts the) 1576 SB
