567 392 1181 (  The ED transient utility lets you create and edit a disk file.) 1181 SB
225 510 1602 (                   The ED utility is a line-oriented context editor.  This means that you) 1602 SB
225 569 1696 (                   create and change character files line-by-line, or by referencing individual) 1696 SB
225 629 716 (                   characters within a line.) 716 SB
225 747 1634 (                   The ED utility lets you create or alter the file named in the file specifi-) 1634 SB
225 806 1456 (                   cation.  Refer to Section 6 for a description of the ED utility.) 1456 SB
225 924 1598 (                   The ED utility uses a portion of your user memory as the active text) 1598 SB
225 984 1676 (                   buffer where you add, delete, or alter the characters in the file.  You use) 1676 SB
225 1043 1646 (                   the A command to read all or a portion of the file into the buffer.  You) 1646 SB
225 1102 1680 (                   use the W or E command to write all or a portion of the characters from) 1680 SB
225 1161 760 (                   the buffer back to the file.) 760 SB
225 1279 1592 (                   An imaginary character pointer, called CP, is at the beginning of the) 1592 SB
225 1339 1664 (                   buffer, between two characters in the buffer, or at the end of the buffer.) 1664 SB
225 1457 1664 (                   You interact with the ED utility in either command or insert mode.  ED) 1664 SB
225 1516 1726 (                   displays the * prompt on the screen when ED is in command mode.  When) 1726 SB
225 1575 1624 (                   the * appears, you can enter the single letter command that reads text) 1624 SB
225 1634 1648 (                   from the buffer,, moves the CP, or changes the ED mode of operation.) 1648 SB
225 1694 1682 (                   When in command mode, you can use the line-editing characters CTRL-) 1682 SB
225 1753 1659 (                   C, CTRL-E, CTRL-H, CTRL-U, CTRL-X, and RUBOUT to edit your) 1659 SB
225 1812 1716 (                   input.  In insert mode, however, you use only CTRL-H, CTRL-U, CTRL-) 1716 SB
225 1871 611 (                   X, and RUBOUT.) 611 SB
1154 2936 92 (5-30) 92 SB
