554 392 1388 ( The ERASE command removes one or more files from a disk's direc-) 1388 SB
225 451 1584 (                 tory in the current user number.  Wildcard characters are accepted in) 1584 SB
225 510 1604 (                 the filespec.  Directory and data space are automatically reclaimed for) 1604 SB
225 569 1614 (                 later use by another file.  The ERASE command can be abbreviated to) 1614 SB
225 629 333 (                 ERA.) 333 SB
225 747 1640 (                 Use the ERASE command with care because all files in the current user) 1640 SB
225 806 1542 (                 number that satisfy the file specification are removed from the disk) 1542 SB
225 865 413 (                 directory.) 413 SB
225 984 895 (                 Command lines that take the form) 895 SB
225 1102 816 (                 ERASE {d:}wlldcard-filespec) 816 SB
225 1220 1586 (                 require your confirmation because they erase an entire group of files,) 1586 SB
225 1279 1534 (                 not 'ust one file.  The system prompts with the following message:) 1534 SB
225 1398 970 (                 ERASE {d:}wildcard-filespec \(Y/N\)?) 970 SB
225 1516 1590 (                 Respond with y if you want to remove all matching files, and n if you) 1590 SB
225 1575 836 (                 want to avoid erasing any files.) 836 SB
225 1694 1595 (                 If no files match the file specification, you see the following message:) 1595 SB
225 1812 382 (                 No Fi le) 382 SB
225 1930 1582 (                 The CONFIRM option informs the system to prompt for verification) 1582 SB
225 1989 1601 (                 before erasing each file that matches the filespec.  You can abbreviate) 1601 SB
225 2049 560 (                 CONFIRM to C.) 560 SB
225 2167 1605 (                 If you use the CONFIRM option with wildcard-filespec, then ERASE) 1605 SB
225 2226 1583 (                 prompts for confirmation for each file.  You can selectively erase the) 1583 SB
225 2285 1562 (                 files you want by responding Y to the confirm message, or keep the) 1562 SB
225 2344 1128 (                 files by responding N to the confirm message.) 1128 SB
1154 2936 92 (5-38) 92 SB
225 77 1929 (The ERASE Command                                                                                CP/M 3 User's Guide) 1929 SB
