554 450 1363 (   The GENCOM command is a transient utility that creates a special) 1363 SB
225 509 1663 (                   COM file with attached RSX files.  RSX files are used as Resident Sys-) 1663 SB
225 568 1583 (                   tem Extensions and are discussed in detail in the CPIM Plus \(CP/M) 1583 SB
225 628 1672 (                   Version 3\) Operating System Programmer's Guide.  GENCOM places a) 1672 SB
225 687 1604 (                   special header at the beginning of the output program file to indicate) 1604 SB
225 746 1579 (                   to the system that RSX loading is required.  It can also set a flag to) 1579 SB
225 805 877 (                   keep the program loader active.) 877 SB
225 923 1618 (                   The GENCOM command can also restore a file already processed by) 1618 SB
225 983 1574 (                   GENCOM to the original COM file without the header and RSXS.) 1574 SB
225 1042 1436 (                   GENCOM has three options that help you attach RSX files:) 1436 SB
225 1160 1637 (                   0  The LOADER option sets a flag to keep the program loader active.) 1637 SB
225 1219 1555 (                      \(For complete details on the LOADER option read about CP/M) 1555 SB
225 1278 1611 (                      function 59 in the CPIM Plus \(CPIM Version 3\) Operating System) 1611 SB
225 1338 1590 (                      Programmer's Guide.\) This option is used only if no RSX files are) 1590 SB
225 1397 794 (                      attached to the COM file.) 794 SB
225 1456 1511 (                   0  The NULL option indicates that only RSX files are specified.) 1511 SB
225 1515 1657 (                      GENCOM creates a dummy COM file for the RSX files.  The output) 1657 SB
225 1574 1612 (                      COM filename is taken from the filename of the first RSX-filespec.) 1612 SB
225 1633 1665 (                   0  The SCB = \(offset,value\) option sets the System Control Block from) 1665 SB
225 1693 1634 (                      the program by using the hex values specified by \(offset,value\).  For) 1634 SB
225 1752 1636 (                      complete details on the SCB option read about CP/M function 49 in) 1636 SB
225 1811 1611 (                      the CPIM Plus \(CPIM Version 3\) Operating System Programmer's) 1611 SB
225 1870 419 (                      Guide.) 419 SB
225 1989 39 (   ) 39 SB
