225 390 1232 (                      GET {CONSOLE INPUT FROM} CONSOLE) 1232 SB
225 509 39 (   ) 39 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c370 font
264 508 303 (  Explanation:) 303 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
567 509 1364 (  The GET command is a transient utility that directs CP/M 3 to take) 1364 SB
225 568 1591 (                   console input from a file.  The file can contain CP/M 3 system com-) 1591 SB
225 628 1689 (                   mands and/or input for a user program.  If you use the SYSTEM option,) 1689 SB
225 687 1508 (                   GET immediately takes the next system command from the file.) 1508 SB
225 805 1625 (                   Console input is taken from a file until the program terminates.  If the) 1625 SB
225 864 1656 (                   file is exhausted before program input is terminated, the program looks) 1656 SB
225 923 1682 (                   for subsequent input from the console.  If the program terminates before) 1682 SB
225 983 1544 (                   exhausting all its input, the system reverts back to the console for) 1544 SB
225 1042 525 (                   console input.) 525 SB
225 1160 1657 (                   When the SYSTEM option is used, the system immediately goes to the) 1657 SB
225 1219 1631 (                   file specified for console input.  If you omit the SYSTEM option, you) 1631 SB
225 1278 1623 (                   can enter one system command to initiate a user program whose con-) 1623 SB
225 1338 1604 (                   sole input is taken from the file specified in the GET command.  The) 1604 SB
225 1397 1614 (                   system reverts to the console for input when it reaches the end of the) 1614 SB
225 1456 1679 (                   GET file input.  The system also reverts to the console for console input) 1679 SB
225 1515 1650 (                   if a GET CONSOLE INPUT FROM CONSOLE command is included) 1650 SB
225 1574 558 (                   in the input file.) 558 SB
225 1694 39 (   ) 39 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c370 font
