958 152 485 (Table 5-7. GET Options) 485 SB
225 270 1078 (                         Option                                  Meaning) 1078 SB
225 389 1604 (                      ECHO                  specifies that the input is echoed to the console.) 1604 SB
225 448 1079 (                                            This is the default option.) 1079 SB
225 566 1664 (                      NO ECHO               specifies that the file input is not to be echoed to) 1664 SB
225 625 1545 (                                            the console.  The program output and the system) 1545 SB
225 685 1501 (                                            prompts are not affected by this option and are) 1501 SB
225 744 1101 (                                            still echoed to the console.) 1101 SB
225 862 1656 (                      SYSTEM                specifies that all system input is to be taken from) 1656 SB
225 921 1537 (                                            the disk file specified in the command line.  GET) 1537 SB
225 980 1560 (                                            takes system and program input from the file until) 1560 SB
225 1040 1494 (                                            the file is exhausted or until GET reads a GET) 1494 SB
225 1099 1198 (                                            console command from the file.) 1198 SB
225 1277 52 (    ) 52 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c370 font
277 1276 248 (  Examples:) 248 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
525 1277 567 (      A> GET FILE XINPUT) 567 SB
225 1336 273 (                     ) 273 SB
525 1336 367 (       A>MYPROG) 367 SB
225 1455 1640 (                     The preceding sequence of commands tells the system to activate the) 1640 SB
225 1514 1657 (                     GET utility.  However, because SYSTEM is not specified, the system) 1657 SB
225 1573 1658 (                     reads the next input line from the console and executes MYPROG.  If) 1658 SB
225 1632 1592 (                     MYPROG program requires console input, it is taken from the file) 1592 SB
225 1691 1670 (                     XINPUT.  When MYPROG terminates, the system reverts to the con-) 1670 SB
225 1751 714 (                     sole for console input.) 714 SB
225 1869 924 (                     A>GET FILE XIN2 [SYSTEM]) 924 SB
225 1987 1650 (                     The preceding command immediately directs the system to get subse-) 1650 SB
225 2046 1639 (                     quent console input from file XIN2 because it includes the SYSTEM) 1639 SB
225 2106 1614 (                     option.  The system reverts to the console for console input when it) 1614 SB
225 2165 1689 (                     reaches the end of file in XIN2.  Or, XIN2 can redirect the system back) 1689 SB
225 2224 1417 (                     to the console if it contains a GET CONSOLE command.) 1417 SB
1154 2934 92 (5-45) 92 SB
225 77 1895 (The GET Command                                                                                  CP/M 3 User's Guide) 1895 SB
