606 569 1359 (  The HELP command is a transient utility that provides summarized) 1359 SB
225 629 1670 (                      information for all of the CP/M 3 commands described in this manual.) 1670 SB
225 688 1670 (                      In the distributed CP/M 3 system, HELP presents general information) 1670 SB
225 747 1667 (                      on a command as a topic and detailed information on a command as a) 1667 SB
225 806 1709 (                      subtopic.  HELP with no command tall displays a list of all the available) 1709 SB
225 865 1633 (                      topics.  HELP with a topic in the command tail displays information) 1633 SB
225 924 1626 (                      about that topic, followed by any available subtopics.  HELP with a) 1626 SB
225 984 1654 (                      topic and a subtopic displays information about the specific subtopic.) 1654 SB
225 1102 1713 (                      After HELP displays the information for your specified topic, it displays) 1713 SB
225 1161 1685 (                      the special prompt HELP> on your screen.  Subtopics can be accessed) 1685 SB
225 1220 1723 (                      by preceding the subtopic with a period.  The period causes the subtopic) 1723 SB
225 1279 1639 (                      search to begin at the last known level.  You can continue to specify) 1639 SB
225 1339 1676 (                      topics for additional information, or simply press the RETURN key to) 1676 SB
225 1398 1023 (                      return to the CP/M 3 system prompt.) 1023 SB
225 1516 1681 (                      You can abbreviate the names of topics and subtopics.  Usually one or) 1681 SB
225 1575 1366 (                      two letters is enough to specifically identify the topics.) 1366 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c370 font
225 1753 536 (        Display Information) 536 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c370 font
225 1871 294 (        Syntax:  ) 294 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
519 1872 1221 (     HELP topic {subtopicl ... subtopic8}{[NO PAGE!LIST]}) 1221 SB
225 1931 746 (                               HELP>.Subtopic) 746 SB
225 2050 1732 (        Explanation:  The preceding forms of the HELP command display the information) 1732 SB
225 2109 1643 (                      for the specified topic and subtopics.  Use the following two options) 1643 SB
225 2168 1050 (                      with this form of the HELP command:) 1050 SB
225 2286 1657 (                      o  The NOPAGE option disables the default paged display of every n) 1657 SB
225 2345 1679 (                         lines, where n is the number of lines per page as set by the system or) 1679 SB
225 2405 1722 (                         as set by the user.  To stop the display, press CTRL-S.  To resume the) 1722 SB
225 2464 1715 (                         display, press CTRL-Q.  You can abbreviate NOPAGE to N. \(See the) 1715 SB
225 2523 1650 (                         DEVICE command for more information about setting the number) 1650 SB
225 2582 682 (                         of lines per page.\)) 682 SB
1154 2937 92 (5-47) 92 SB
