329 152 290 ( Explanation:) 290 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
619 153 1382 (  CP/M 3 is distributed with two related HELP files: HELP.COM and) 1382 SB
225 212 1663 (                       HELP.HLP. The HELP.COM file is the command file that processes) 1663 SB
225 271 1582 (                       the text of the HELP.HLP file and displays it on the screen.  The) 1582 SB
225 331 1706 (                       HELP.HLP file is a text file to which you can add customized informa-) 1706 SB
225 390 1728 (                       tion, but you cannot directly edit the HELP.HLP file.  You must use the) 1728 SB
225 449 1645 (                       HELP.COM file to convert HELP.HLP to a file named HELP.DAT) 1645 SB
225 508 1126 (                       before you can edit or add your own text.) 1126 SB
225 626 1492 (                       This form of the HELP command has the following options:) 1492 SB
225 745 1671 (                       o  The EXTRACT option accesses the file HELP.HLP on the default) 1671 SB
225 804 1689 (                          drive and creates a file called HELP.DAT on the default drive.  You) 1689 SB
225 863 1694 (                          can now invoke a word processing program to edit or add your own) 1694 SB
225 922 1631 (                          text to the HELP.DAT file.  EXTRACT can be abbreviated to E.) 1631 SB
225 981 1658 (                       o  The CREATE option accesses your edited HELP.DAT file on the) 1658 SB
225 1041 1721 (                          default drive and builds a revised HELP.HLP file on the default drive.) 1721 SB
225 1100 1027 (                          CREATE can be abbreviated to C.) 1027 SB
225 1218 1697 (                       You must add topics and subtopics to the HELP.DAT file in a specific) 1697 SB
225 1277 1547 (                       format.  A topic heading in the HELP.DAT file takes the form:) 1547 SB
225 1396 681 (                       ///nTopicname<cr>) 681 SB
225 1514 1651 (                       The three backslashes are the topic delimiters and must begin in col-) 1651 SB
225 1573 1717 (                       umn one.  In the preceding format statement, n is a number in the range) 1717 SB
225 1632 1616 (                       from 1 through 9 that signifies the level of the topic.  A main topic) 1616 SB
225 1691 1660 (                       always has a level number of 1. The first subtopic has a level number) 1660 SB
225 1751 1669 (                       of 2. The next level of subtopic has a level number of 3, and so forth,) 1669 SB
225 1810 1698 (                       up to a maximum of nine levels.  Topicname is the name of your topic,) 1698 SB
225 1869 1666 (                       and allows a maximum of twelve characters.  The entire line is termi-) 1666 SB
225 1928 860 (                       nated with a carriage return.) 860 SB
225 2046 1715 (                       Use the following guidelines to edit and insert text into the HELP.DAT) 1715 SB
225 2106 373 (                       file.) 373 SB
225 2224 1272 (                      o    Topics should be placed in alphabetical order.) 1272 SB
225 2283 1638 (                      o    Subtopics should be placed alphabetically within their respective) 1638 SB
225 2342 598 (                             supertopic.) 598 SB
225 2401 1203 (                      o    Levels must be indicated by a number 1-9.) 1203 SB
1154 2934 92 (5-49) 92 SB
225 77 1896 (The HELP Command                                                                               CP/M 3 User's Guide ) 1896 SB
EJ RS
