525 629 1431 (A library file contains a collection of object modules. Use the LIB utility) 1431 SB
225 688 1622 (                      to create libraries, and to append, replace, select, or delete modules) 1622 SB
225 747 1650 (                      from an existing library.  You can also use LIB to obtain information) 1650 SB
225 806 952 (                      about the contents of library files.) 952 SB
225 924 1644 (                      LIB creates and maintains library files that contain object modules in) 1644 SB
225 984 1605 (                      MicroSoft@ REL format.  These modules are produced by Digital) 1605 SB
225 1043 1692 (                      Research's relocatable macro-assembler program, RMAC, or any other) 1692 SB
225 1102 1659 (                      language translator that produces modules in MicroSoft REL format.) 1659 SB
225 1220 1583 (                      LINK-80" links the object modules contained in a library to other) 1583 SB
225 1279 1681 (                      ob'ect files.  LINK-80 automatically selects from the library only those) 1681 SB
225 1339 337 (                         i) 337 SB
225 1398 1653 (                      modules needed by the program being linked, and then forms an exe-) 1653 SB
225 1457 989 (                      cutable file with a filetype of COM.) 989 SB
225 1575 1639 (                      The library file has the filetype REL or IRL depending on the option) 1639 SB
225 1634 1680 (                      you choose.  Modules in a REL library file must not contain backward) 1680 SB
225 1694 1665 (                      references to modules that occur earlier in the library, because LINK-) 1665 SB
225 1753 1302 (                      80 currently makes only one pass through a library.) 1302 SB
1148 2936 105 (5-5 3) 105 SB
225 77 1877 (The LIB Command                                                                                  CP/M 3 User's Guide) 1877 SB
