375 568 1518 (       The LINK command combines relocatable ob'ect modules such as those) 1518 SB
225 628 1596 (                   produced by RMAC and PL/1-80" into a COM file ready for execu-) 1596 SB
225 687 1744 (                  tion.  Relocatable files can contain external references and publics.  Relocat-) 1744 SB
225 746 1696 (                  able files can reference modules in library files.  LINK searches the library) 1696 SB
225 805 1634 (                  files and includes the referenced modules in the output file.  The LINK) 1634 SB
225 864 1648 (                  command is the LINK-80 utility and are synonymous in this discussion.) 1648 SB
225 923 1616 (                  See the Programmer's Utilities Guide for the CPIM Family of Operat-) 1616 SB
225 983 1268 (                  ing Systems for a complete description of LINK-80.) 1268 SB
225 1101 1654 (                  You can use LINK option switches to control the execution parameters) 1654 SB
225 1160 1701 (                  of LINK-80.  LINK options follow the file specifications and are enclosed) 1701 SB
225 1219 1592 (                  within square brackets.  Multiple switches are separated by commas.) 1592 SB
225 1397 1076 (                                          Table 5-10. LINK Options) 1076 SB
225 1515 1026 (                    Option                                   Meaning) 1026 SB
225 1633 1536 (                    A                Additional memory; reduces buffer space and writes) 1536 SB
225 1693 943 (                                     temporary data to disk.) 943 SB
225 1811 1473 (                    B                BIOS link in banked CP/M 3 system. Aligns data) 1473 SB
225 1870 1517 (                                     segment on page boundary; puts length of code seg-) 1517 SB
225 1929 1282 (                                     ment in header; defaults to SPR filetype.) 1282 SB
225 2048 1517 (                    Dbhhh            Data origin; sets memory origin for common and) 1517 SB
225 2107 674 (                                     data area.) 674 SB
225 2225 1131 (                    Gn               Go; set start address to label n.) 1131 SB
