225 152 839 (   Examples:     A>LINK B:MYFILE[NR]) 839 SB
225 270 1605 (                 LINK-80 on drive A uses as input MYFILE.REL on drive B and pro-) 1605 SB
225 330 1638 (                 duces the executable machine code file MYFILE.COM on drive B. The) 1638 SB
225 389 1058 (                 [NR] option specifies no symbol table file.) 1058 SB
225 507 640 (                 A>LINK ml ,m2, m3) 640 SB
225 625 1687 (                 LINK-80 combines the separately compiled files ml, m2, and m3, resolves) 1687 SB
225 685 1651 (                 their external references', and produces the executable machine code file) 1651 SB
225 744 409 (                 ml.COM.) 409 SB
225 862 718 (                 A>LINK m=m1, m2, m3) 718 SB
225 980 1584 (                 LINK-80 combines the separately compiled files ml, m2, and m3 and) 1584 SB
225 1040 1253 (                 produces the executable machine code file M.COM.) 1253 SB
225 1158 796 (                 A>LINK MYFILE,FILE5[s]) 796 SB
225 1276 1585 (                 The [s] option tells LINK-80 to search FILE5 as a library.  LINK-80) 1585 SB
225 1335 1602 (                 combines MYFILE.REL with the referenced subroutines contained in) 1602 SB
225 1395 1570 (                 FILE5.REL on the default drive A and produces MYFILE.COM on) 1570 SB
225 1454 382 (                 drive A.) 382 SB
1154 2933 92 (5-58) 92 SB
