593 391 26 (  ) 26 SB
375 450 1421 (         MAC, the CP/M Macro Assembler, is a transient utility that reads) 1421 SB
225 509 1659 (                     assembly language statements from a disk file of filetype ASM.  MAC) 1659 SB
225 568 1682 (                     assembles the statements and produces three output files with the input) 1682 SB
225 628 1369 (                     filename and output filetypes of HEX, PRN, and SYM.) 1369 SB
225 746 1649 (                     Filename.HEX contains IntelO hexadecimal format ob'ect code.  You) 1649 SB
225 805 1684 (                     can debug the HEX file with a debugger, or use HEX COM to create a) 1684 SB
225 864 762 (                     COM file and execute it.) 762 SB
225 983 1663 (                     Filename.PRN contains an annotated source listing that can be printed) 1663 SB
225 1042 1648 (                     or examined at the console.  The PRN file includes a 16-column wide) 1648 SB
225 1101 1567 (                     listing at the left side of the page that shows the values of literals,) 1567 SB
225 1160 1645 (                     machine code addresses, and generated machine code.  An equal sign) 1645 SB
225 1219 1589 (                     denotes literal addresses to eliminate confusion with machine code) 1589 SB
225 1278 476 (                     addresses.) 476 SB
225 1397 1695 (                     Filename.SYM contains a sorted list of symbols defined in the program.) 1695 SB
225 1515 1625 (                     Before invoking MAC, you must prepare a source program file with) 1625 SB
225 1574 1449 (                     the filetype ASM containing assembly language statements.) 1449 SB
225 1693 1632 (                     You can direct the input and output of MAC using the options listed) 1632 SB
225 1752 1569 (                     in the following table.  Use a letter with the option to indicate the) 1569 SB
225 1811 1643 (                     source and destination drives, console, printer, or zero output.  Valid) 1643 SB
225 1870 1694 (                     drive names are A through 0. X directs output to the console.  P directs) 1694 SB
225 1929 1646 (                     output to the printer.  Z specifies that output files will not be created.) 1646 SB
1154 2935 92 (5-59) 92 SB
225 77 1883 (The MAC Command                                                                                CP/M 3 User's Guide) 1883 SB
