225 1693 1731 (                       source.  PIP copies the files specified in the source from left to right and) 1731 SB
225 1752 1692 (                       combines them into one file with the name indicated by the destination) 1692 SB
225 1811 1781 (                       file specification.  This procedure is called file concatenation.  You can use) 1781 SB
225 1870 1680 (                       the [Gn] option after the destination file to place it in the user number) 1680 SB
225 1929 1736 (                       specified by n. You can specify one or more options for each source file.) 1736 SB
225 2048 1697 (                       Some of the options force PIP to copy files character-by-character.  In) 1697 SB
225 2107 1698 (                       these cases, PIP looks for a CTRL-Z character to determine where the) 1698 SB
