225 152 1334 (                    You can terminate PIP operations by typing CTRL-C.) 1334 SB
225 270 1665 (                    When concatenating files, PIP only searches the last record of a file for) 1665 SB
375 330 1516 (        the CTRL-Z end-of-file character. However, if PIP is doing a character) 1516 SB
225 389 1400 (                    transfer, it stops when it encounters a CTRL-Z character.) 1400 SB
225 507 1700 (                    Use the [O] option if you are concatenating machine code files.  The [O]) 1700 SB
225 566 1693 (                    option causes PIP to ignore embedded CTRL-Z \(end-of-file\) characters,) 1693 SB
225 625 1649 (                    which indicate the end-of-file character in text files, but might be valid) 1649 SB
225 685 741 (                    data in object code files.) 741 SB
