225 152 1190 (                     The logical device names are listed as follows:) 1190 SB
225 270 1716 (                     o  CON: Console input or output device. When used as a source, usually) 1716 SB
225 330 1514 (                        the keyboard; when used as a destination, usually the screen.) 1514 SB
225 389 1134 (                     o  AUX: Auxiliary Input or Output Device.) 1134 SB
225 448 1715 (                     o  LST: The destination device assigned to the list output device, usually) 1715 SB
225 507 531 (                        the printer.) 531 SB
225 625 1386 (                     The following three device names have special meaning:) 1386 SB
225 744 1508 (                     o  NUL: A source device that produces 40 hexadecimal zeros.) 1508 SB
225 803 1654 (                     o  EOF: A source device that produces a single CTRL-Z, the CP/M 3) 1654 SB
225 862 646 (                        end-of-file mark.) 646 SB
225 921 1678 (                     o  PRN: The printer device with tab expansion to every eighth column,) 1678 SB
225 980 1265 (                        line numbers, and page ejects every sixtieth line.) 1265 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c370 font
225 1099 313 (      Examples: ) 313 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
538 1100 802 (     B>PIP PRN:=CON:MYDATA.DAT) 802 SB
225 1218 1629 (                     Characters are first read from the console input device, generally the) 1629 SB
225 1277 1691 (                     keyboard, and sent directly to your printer device.  You type a CI'RL-Z) 1691 SB
225 1336 1684 (                     character to tell PIP that keyboard input is complete.  At that time, PIP) 1684 SB
225 1396 1639 (                     continues by reading character data from the file MYDATA.DAT on) 1639 SB
225 1455 1699 (                     drive B. Because PRN: is the destination device, tabs are expanded, line) 1699 SB
225 1514 1443 (                     numbers are added, and page ejects occur every sixty lines.) 1443 SB
225 1632 1673 (                     Note that when the CON: device is the source you must enter both the) 1673 SB
225 1691 1583 (                     carriage return \(RETURN\) and line-feed \(LF\) keys for a new line.) 1583 SB
225 1810 954 (                     A>PIP B:FUNFILE.SUE = CON:) 954 SB
225 1928 1726 (                     Whatever you type at the console is written to the file FUNFILE.SUE on) 1726 SB
225 1987 1342 (                     drive B. End the keyboard input by typing a CTRL-Z.) 1342 SB
225 2106 672 (                     A>PIP LST:=CON:) 672 SB
225 2224 1685 (                     Whatever you type at the console keyboard is written to the list device,) 1685 SB
225 2283 1361 (                     generally the printer.  Terminate input with a CTRL-Z.) 1361 SB
1154 2934 92 (5-69) 92 SB
