375 746 1444 (         The PUT command is a transient utility that lets you direct console) 1444 SB
225 805 1675 (                     output or printer output to a file.  PUT allows you to direct the system) 1675 SB
225 864 1599 (                     to put console output or printer output to a file for the next system) 1599 SB
225 923 1665 (                     command or user program entered at the console.  Or, PUT directs all) 1665 SB
225 983 1600 (                     subsequent console or printer output to a file when you include the) 1600 SB
225 1042 625 (                     SYSTEM option.) 625 SB
225 1160 1687 (                     Console output is directed to a file until the program terminates.  Then,) 1687 SB
225 1219 1707 (                     console output reverts to the console.  Printer output is directed to a file) 1707 SB
225 1278 1641 (                     until the program terminates.  Then printer output is directed back to) 1641 SB
225 1338 492 (                     the printer.) 492 SB
225 1456 1692 (                     When you use the SYSTEM option, all subsequent console/printer out-) 1692 SB
225 1515 1634 (                     put is directed to the specified file.  This option terminates when you) 1634 SB
225 1574 1428 (                     enter the PUT CONSOLE or PLTT PRINTER command.) 1428 SB
225 1693 891 (                     The syntax for the option list is) 891 SB
225 1811 1550 (                     [{ECHO | NO ECHO} {FILTER | NO FILTER} | {SYSTEM}]) 1550 SB
225 1929 1147 (                     Table 5-14 defines the preceding option list.) 1147 SB
1148 2935 105 ( 5-77) 105 SB
225 77 1918 (The PUT Command                                                                                    CP/M 3 User's Guide) 1918 SB
