632 391 1353 (   The RENAME command lets you change the name of a file that is) 1353 SB
225 450 1648 (                         cataloged in the directory of a disk.  It also lets you change several) 1648 SB
225 509 1647 (                         filenames if you use wildcards in the filespecs.  You can abbreviate) 1647 SB
225 568 715 (                         RENAME to REN.) 715 SB
225 687 1721 (                         The new-filespec must not be the name of any existing file on the disk.) 1721 SB
225 746 1527 (                         The old-filespec identifies an existing file or files on the disk.) 1527 SB
225 864 1723 (                         The RENAME command changes the file named by old-filespec to the) 1723 SB
225 923 878 (                         name given as new-filespec.) 878 SB
225 1042 1701 (                         RENAME does not make a copy of the file.  RENAME changes only) 1701 SB
225 1101 719 (                         the name of the file.) 719 SB
225 1219 1728 (                         If you omit the drive specifier, RENAME assumes the file to rename is) 1728 SB
225 1278 1709 (                         on the default drive.  You can include a drive specifier as a part of the) 1709 SB
225 1338 1713 (                         newname.  If both file specifications name a drive, it must be the same) 1713 SB
225 1397 438 (                         drive.) 438 SB
225 1515 1634 (                         If the file given by oldname does not exist, RENAME displays the) 1634 SB
225 1574 982 (                         following message on the screen:) 982 SB
225 1693 473 (                         No File) 473 SB
225 1811 1793 (                         If the file given by newname is already present in the directory, RENAME) 1793 SB
225 1870 1226 (                         displays the following message on the screen:) 1226 SB
225 1988 1193 (                         Not renamed filename.typ file already exists) 1193 SB
225 2048 658 (                         delete \( Y/N     ?) 658 SB
225 2166 1710 (                         If you want to delete the old file, type Y to delete.  Otherwise, type N) 1710 SB
225 2225 1272 (                         to keep the old file and not rename the new file.) 1272 SB
1154 2935 92 (5-81) 92 SB
