554 392 1366 (  RMAC is a relocatable macro assembler that assembles files of type) 1366 SB
225 451 1412 (                  ASM into REL files that can be linked to create COM files.) 1412 SB
225 569 1561 (                  The RMAC command options specify the destination of the output) 1561 SB
225 629 1551 (                  files.  The additional specifier d defines the destination drive of the) 1551 SB
225 688 1613 (                  output files.  A-0 specifies drives A through 0. X means output to the) 1613 SB
225 747 1664 (                  console, P means output to the printer, and Z means zero output.  Table) 1664 SB
225 806 1027 (                  5-15 lists the RMAC command options.) 1027 SB
225 924 1229 (                                  Table 5-15.  RMAC Command Options) 1229 SB
225 984 1269 (                                   Option                          d =output option) 1269 SB
225 1102 1213 (                            R drive for REL file                     \(A-O, Z\)) 1213 SB
225 1161 1338 (                            S drive for SYM file                     \(A-O, X, P, Z\)) 1338 SB
225 1220 1340 (                            P drive for PRN file                      \(A-O, X, P, Z\)) 1340 SB
225 1398 1617 (                  In the MAC command, the assembly parameter of H controls the des-) 1617 SB
225 1457 1559 (                  tination of the HEX file.  In the RMAC command this parameter is) 1559 SB
225 1516 1647 (                  replaced by R, which controls the destination of the REL file; however,) 1647 SB
225 1575 1566 (                  you cannot direct the REL file to the console or printer, RX or RP,) 1566 SB
225 1634 1056 (                  because the REL file is not an ASCII file.) 1056 SB
225 1753 920 (    Examples:     A>RMAC TEST $PX SB RB) 920 SB
225 1871 1610 (                  In the preceding example RMAC assembles the file TEST.ASM from) 1610 SB
225 1930 1551 (                  drive A, sends the listing file \(TEST.PRN\) to the console, puts the) 1551 SB
225 1989 1652 (                  symbol file \(TEST.SYM\) on drive B and puts the relocatable object file) 1652 SB
225 2049 731 (                  \(TEST.REL\) on drive B.) 731 SB
1154 2936 92 (5-84) 92 SB
225 77 1916 (The RMAC Command                                                                                CP/M 3 User's Guide) 1916 SB
EJ RS
