554 509 1426 (  The SET command initiates password protection and time stamping of) 1426 SB
225 568 1633 (                  files in the CP/M 3 system. It also sets file and drive attributes, such as) 1633 SB
225 628 1593 (                  the Read-Only, SYS, and user-definable attributes. It lets you label a) 1593 SB
225 687 948 (                  disk and password protect the label.) 948 SB
225 805 1595 (                  The SET command include options that affect the disk directory, the) 1595 SB
225 864 1553 (                  drive, or a file or set of files.  The discussion of the SET command) 1553 SB
225 923 1383 (                  explicitly states which of the three categories are affected.) 1383 SB
225 1042 1646 (                  To enable time stamping of files, you must first run INITDIR to format) 1646 SB
225 1101 594 (                  the disk directory.) 594 SB
