619 153 1410 ( You can assign one of four modes of password protection to your file.) 1410 SB
225 212 1703 (                        The protection modes are READ, WRITE, DELETE, and NONE and) 1703 SB
225 271 1019 (                        are described in the following table.) 1019 SB
225 390 1336 (                                        Table 5-17.  Password Protection Modes) 1336 SB
225 449 1130 (                           Mode                                   Protection) 1130 SB
225 567 1596 (                          READ               The password is required for reading, copying,) 1596 SB
225 626 1335 (                                             writing, deleting, or renaming the file.) 1335 SB
225 745 1656 (                          WRITE              The password is required for writing, deleting, or) 1656 SB
225 804 1581 (                                             renaming the file.  You do not need a password to) 1581 SB
225 863 832 (                                             read the file.) 832 SB
225 981 1662 (                          DELETE             The password is only required for deleting or re-) 1662 SB
225 1041 1542 (                                             naming the file.  You do not need a password to) 1542 SB
225 1100 1039 (                                             read or modify the file.) 1039 SB
225 1218 1711 (                          NONE               No password exists for the file. If a password exists,) 1711 SB
225 1277 1552 (                                             this modifier can be used to delete the password.) 1552 SB
225 1456 130 (          ) 130 SB
