593 807 1411 (  The preceding SET commands allow you to keep a record of the time) 1411 SB
225 866 1675 (                     and date of file creation and update, or of the last access and update of) 1675 SB
225 925 470 (                     your files.) 470 SB
225 1044 1680 (                     [CREATE     ON]           turns on CREATE time stamps on the disk in) 1680 SB
225 1103 1518 (                                               the default drive.  To record the creation time) 1518 SB
225 1162 1515 (                                               of a file, the CREATE option must have been) 1515 SB
225 1221 1304 (                                               turned on before the file is created.) 1304 SB
225 1340 1683 (                     [ACCESS = ON]             turns on ACCESS time stamps on the disk in) 1683 SB
225 1399 1452 (                                               the default drive.  ACCESS and CREATE) 1452 SB
225 1458 1562 (                                               options are mutually exclusive.  This means that) 1562 SB
225 1517 1530 (                                               only one can be in effect at a time.  If you turn) 1530 SB
225 1576 1525 (                                               on the ACCESS time stamp on a disk that has) 1525 SB
225 1635 1502 (                                               the CREATE time stamp, the CREATE time) 1502 SB
225 1695 1274 (                                               stamp is automatically turned off.) 1274 SB
225 1813 1701 (                     [UPDATE = ON]             turns on UPDATE time stamps on the disk in) 1701 SB
225 1872 1510 (                                               the default drive.  UPDATE time stamps rec-) 1510 SB
225 1931 1371 (                                               ord the time the file was last modified.) 1371 SB
225 2050 1620 (                     To enable time stamping', you must first run INITDIR to format the) 1620 SB
225 2109 1102 (                     disk directory for time and date stamping.) 1102 SB
225 2227 1676 (                     Although there are three kinds of date/time stamps, only two date/time) 1676 SB
225 2286 1689 (                     stamps can be associated with a given file at one time.  You can choose) 1689 SB
225 2345 1701 (                     to have either a CREATE date or an ACCESS date for files on a partic-) 1701 SB
225 2405 456 (                     ular disk.) 456 SB
