606 509 1441 ( The SETDEF command lets you display or define the disk search order,) 1441 SB
225 568 1706 (                     the temporary drive, and the filetype search order.  The SETDEF defini-) 1706 SB
225 628 1681 (                     tions affect only the loading of programs and/or execution of SUBMIT) 1681 SB
225 687 1800 (                     \(SUB\) files.  The SETDEF command also lets you turn on/off the DISPLAY) 1800 SB
225 746 1765 (                     and PAGE modes for the system.  When DISPLAY mode is on, the system) 1765 SB
225 805 1740 (                     displays the location and name of programs loaded or SUB files executed.) 1740 SB
225 864 1678 (                     When PAGE mode is on, CP/M 3 utilities stop after displaying one full) 1678 SB
225 923 1480 (                     screen of information.  Press any key to continue the display.) 1480 SB
225 1042 1666 (                     The system usually searches the specified drive or the default drive for) 1666 SB
225 1101 1698 (                     files.  The user can use the SETDEF command, to extend the search for) 1698 SB
225 1160 1448 (                     program files and submit files, for execution purposes only.) 1448 SB
225 1278 1679 (                     Note: A CP/M 3 program file has a filetype of COM.  A file containing) 1679 SB
225 1338 1499 (                     commands to be executed by SUBMIT has a filetype of SUB.) 1499 SB
