593 392 1388 ( The SID \(Symbolic Instruction Debugger\) allows you to monitor and) 1388 SB
225 451 1630 (                    test programs developed for the 8080 microprocessor.  SID supports) 1630 SB
225 510 1676 (                    real-time breakpoints, fully monitored execution, symbolic disassembly,) 1676 SB
225 569 1643 (                    assembly, and memory display and fill functions.  Utility programs are) 1643 SB
225 629 1564 (                    supplied with CP/M 3 that can be dynamically loaded with SID to) 1564 SB
225 688 1098 (                    provide traceback and histogram facilities.) 1098 SB
225 806 1691 (                    SID commands display memory and CPU registers and direct the break-) 1691 SB
225 865 1185 (                    point operations during the debugging session.) 1185 SB
225 984 1652 (                    Without a file specification SID loads into memory without a test pro-) 1652 SB
225 1043 1606 (                    gram.  Use this form to examine memory or to write and test simple) 1606 SB
225 1102 1679 (                    programs using the A command.  You must not use the SID commands) 1679 SB
225 1161 1642 (                    G, T, or U, described later, until you have first loaded a test program.) 1642 SB
225 1279 1634 (                    A SID command line with a pgm-filespec loads both SID and the test) 1634 SB
225 1339 1690 (                    program into memory.  If the filetype is omitted from the filespec, COM) 1690 SB
225 1398 1696 (                    is assumed.  SID optionally loads in a symbol table file specified by sym-) 1696 SB
225 1457 1694 (                    filespec.  The sym-filespec needs no filetype because SID looks for a file) 1694 SB
225 1516 1685 (                    with filetype SYM.  Use the C, G, T, or U command to begin execution) 1685 SB
225 1575 1166 (                    of the test program under supervision of SID.) 1166 SB
225 1694 1642 (                    Use CTRL-S to halt the screen display.  CTRL-Q restarts the display.) 1642 SB
225 1753 1683 (                    Abort lengthy displays by typing any keyboard character.  Use CTRL-C) 1683 SB
225 1812 602 (                    to exit from SID.) 602 SB
225 1930 1644 (                    SID can address absolute memory locations through symbolic expres-) 1644 SB
225 1989 1629 (                    sions.  A symbolic expression evaluates to either an address or a data) 1629 SB
225 2049 359 (                    item.) 359 SB
1141 2936 117 (5-103) 117 SB
225 77 1904 (The SID Command                                                                                    CP/M 3 User's Guide) 1904 SB
