225 152 1621 (                   The HIST utility creates a histogram \(bar graph\) showing the relative) 1621 SB
225 211 1677 (                   frequency of execution of code within selected program segments of the) 1677 SB
225 270 1664 (                   test program.  The HIST utility allows you to monitor those sections of) 1664 SB
225 330 932 (                   code that execute most frequently.) 932 SB
225 448 828 (                   Upon start-up HIST prompts) 828 SB
225 566 900 (                   TYPE HISTOGRAM BOUNDS) 900 SB
225 685 1085 (                   Enter the bounds in the following format-,) 1085 SB
225 803 444 (                   aaaa,bbbb) 444 SB
225 921 1579 (                   for a histogram between locations aaaa and bbbb inclusive.  Collect) 1579 SB
225 980 1069 (                   data in U or T mode, then display results.) 1069 SB
225 1099 1642 (                   The TRACE utility obtains a traceback of the instructions that led to a) 1642 SB
225 1158 1650 (                   particular breakpoint address in a program under test.  You can collect) 1650 SB
225 1217 1621 (                   the addresses of up to 256 instructions between pass points in U or T) 1621 SB
225 1276 389 (                   modes.) 389 SB
