303 152 544 ( The SUBMIT Command) 544 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c370 font
225 272 268 (       Syntax: ) 268 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
493 273 1038 (       SUBMIT {filespec} {argument} ... {argument}) 1038 SB
225 392 78 (      ) 78 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c370 font
303 391 303 ( Explanation: ) 303 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
606 392 1355 (  The SUBMIT command lets you execute a group or batch of com-) 1355 SB
225 451 1473 (                      mands from a SUB file, which is a file with filetype of SUB.) 1473 SB
225 569 1679 (                      Usually, you enter commands one line at a time.  If you must enter the) 1679 SB
225 629 1664 (                      same sequence of commands several times, you might find it easier to) 1664 SB
225 688 1727 (                      batch the commands together using the SUBMIT command.  To do this,) 1727 SB
225 747 1678 (                      create a file and enter your commands in this file.  The file is identified) 1678 SB
225 806 1681 (                      by the filename, and must have a filetype of SUB.  When you issue the) 1681 SB
225 865 1685 (                      SUBMIT command, SUBMIT reads the file named by the filespec and) 1685 SB
225 924 1692 (                      prepares it for interpretation by CP/M 3. When the preparation is com-) 1692 SB
225 984 1629 (                      plete, SUBMIT sends the file to CP/M 3 line-by-line, as if you were) 1629 SB
225 1043 732 (                      typing each command.) 732 SB
225 1161 1675 (                      The SUBMIT command executes the commands from a SUB file as if) 1675 SB
225 1220 1299 (                      you are entering the commands from the keyboard.) 1299 SB
225 1339 1625 (                      You create the SUB file with the ED utility.  It can contain CP/M 3) 1625 SB
225 1398 1662 (                      commands, nested SUBMIT commands, and input data for a CP/M 3) 1662 SB
225 1457 765 (                      command or a program.) 765 SB
225 1575 1648 (                      You can pass arguments to SUB files when you execute them.  Each) 1648 SB
225 1634 1713 (                      argument you enter is assigned to a parameter in the SUB file.  The first) 1713 SB
225 1694 1671 (                      argument replaces every occurrence of $1 in the file, the second argu-) 1671 SB
225 1753 1675 (                      ment replaces parameter $2, etc., up to parameter $9.  For example, if) 1675 SB
225 1812 1423 (                      your file START.SUB contains the following commands:) 1423 SB
225 1930 564 (                      ERA $1.BAK) 564 SB
225 1989 435 (                      DIR $1) 435 SB
225 2049 701 (                      PIP $1 =A: $2.COM) 701 SB
225 2167 1254 (                      and you enter the following SUBMIT command:) 1254 SB
225 2285 953 (                      A> SUBMIT START SAM TEX) 953 SB
1141 2936 117 (5-109) 117 SB
225 77 1882 (The SUBMIT Command                                                                          CP/M 3 User's Guide) 1882 SB
EJ RS
