225 744 1664 (                     Every time you turn on or reset your computer, CP/M 3 automatically) 1664 SB
225 803 1721 (                     looks for a special SUB file named PROFILE.SUB to execute.  If it does) 1721 SB
225 862 1721 (                     not exist, then CP/M 3 resumes normal operation.  If the PROFILE.SUB) 1721 SB
225 921 1616 (                     file exists, the system executes the commands in the file.  This file is) 1616 SB
225 980 1623 (                     convenient to use if you regularly execute a set of commands before) 1623 SB
225 1040 1697 (                     you do your regular session on the computer.  For example, if you want) 1697 SB
225 1099 1581 (                     to be sure that you always enter the current date and time on your) 1581 SB
225 1158 1613 (                     computer before you enter any other commands, you can create the) 1613 SB
225 1217 1715 (                     PROFILE.SUB file, with ED, and enter the DATE command as follows:) 1715 SB
225 1335 509 (                     DATE SET) 509 SB
225 1454 1717 (                     Then, whenever you bring up the system, the system executes the DATE) 1717 SB
225 1513 1631 (                     command and prompts you to enter the date and time.  By using this) 1631 SB
225 1572 1622 (                     facility, you can be sure to execute a regular sequence of commands) 1622 SB
225 1631 948 (                     before starting your usual session.) 948 SB
1141 2933 117 (5-113) 117 SB
