567 451 1398 (  The TYPE command displays the contents of an ASCII character file) 1398 SB
225 510 1661 (                   on your screen.  The PAGE option displays the console listing in paged) 1661 SB
225 569 1596 (                   mode, which means that the console listing stops automatically after) 1596 SB
225 629 1617 (                   listing n lines of text, where n is usually the system default of 24 lines) 1617 SB
225 688 1587 (                   per page. \(See the DEVICE command to set n to a different value.\)) 1587 SB
225 747 1588 (                   Press any character to continue listing another n lines of text.  Press) 1588 SB
225 806 1518 (                   CTRL-C to exit back to the system.  PAGE is the default mode.) 1518 SB
225 924 1512 (                   The NO PAGE option displays the console listing continuously.) 1512 SB
225 1043 1681 (                   If you do not enter a file specification in the TYPE command the system) 1681 SB
225 1102 1063 (                   prompts for a filename with the message:) 1063 SB
225 1220 770 (                   Enter filename :                ) 770 SB
225 1279 507 (                                       ) 507 SB
225 1339 1287 (                   Respond with the filespec of the file you want listed.) 1287 SB
225 1457 1625 (                   Tab characters occurring in the file named by the file specification are) 1625 SB
225 1516 1387 (                   expanded to every eighth column position of your screen.) 1387 SB
225 1634 1652 (                   At any time during the display, you can interrupt the listing by pressing) 1652 SB
225 1694 1184 (                   CTRL-S.  Press CTRL-Q to resume the listing.) 1184 SB
225 1812 1077 (                   Press CTRL-C to exit back to the system.) 1077 SB
225 1930 1580 (                   Make sure the file specification identifies a file containing character) 1580 SB
225 1989 344 (                   data.) 344 SB
225 2108 1642 (                   If the file named by the file specification is not present on the specified) 1642 SB
225 2167 1443 (                   drive, TYPE displays the following message on your screen:) 1443 SB
225 2285 395 (                   No File) 395 SB
1141 2936 117 (5-114) 117 SB
