225 862 1605 (      The second form of the I command does not enter insert mode.  It inserts the) 1605 SB
225 921 1697 (    character string into the memory buffer and returns immediately to the ED prompt.) 1697 SB
225 980 1660 (    You can use CP/M 3's line-editing control characters to edit the command string.) 1660 SB
225 1099 1682 (      To insert a string, first use one of the commands that position the CP.  You must) 1682 SB
225 1158 1647 (    move the CP to the place where vou want to insert a string.  For example, if you) 1647 SB
225 1217 1671 (    want to insert a string at the beginning of the first line, use a B command to move) 1671 SB
225 1276 1656 (    the CP to the beginning of the buffer.  With the CP positioned correctly, enter an) 1656 SB
225 1335 512 (    insert string, as follows) 512 SB
225 1454 297 (    iIn 1870, ^Z) 297 SB
