225 1276 1754 (         It saves keystrokes and editing time to combine the editing and display commands.) 1754 SB
225 1335 1657 (       You can type any number of ED commands on the same line.  ED executes the) 1657 SB
225 1395 1688 (       command string only after you press the carriage return key.  Use CP/M 3's line-) 1688 SB
225 1454 1126 (       editing controls to manipulate ED command strings.) 1126 SB
225 1572 1681 (         When you combine several commands on a line, ED executes them in the same) 1681 SB
225 1631 1638 (       order they are entered, from left to right on the command line.  There are four) 1638 SB
225 1690 903 (       restrictions to combining ED commands:) 903 SB
225 1809 1601 (           o   The combined-command line must not exceed CP/M 3's 128 character) 1601 SB
225 1868 402 (               maximum.) 402 SB
225 1927 1702 (           o   If the combined-command line contains a character string, the line must not) 1702 SB
225 1986 648 (               exceed 100 characters.) 648 SB
225 2045 1684 (           o   Commands to terminate an editing session must not appear in a combined-) 1684 SB
225 2105 484 (               command line.) 484 SB
225 2164 1693 (           o   Commands, such as the 1, J, R, S, and X commands, that require character) 1693 SB
225 2223 1622 (               strings or filespecs must be either the last command on a line or must be) 1622 SB
225 2282 1683 (               terminated with a CTRL-Z or ESC character, even if no character string or) 1683 SB
225 2341 521 (               filespec is given.) 521 SB
