225 567 577 (     The P \(Page\) Command) 577 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
225 686 1671 (      Although you can display any amount of text at the screen with a T command, it) 1671 SB
225 745 1722 (     is sometimes more convenient to page through the buffer, viewing whole screens of) 1722 SB
225 804 1732 (     data and moving the CP to the top of each new screen at the same time.  To do this,) 1732 SB
225 863 1380 (     use ED's P command.  The P command takes the following forms:) 1380 SB
225 981 264 (         nP, -nP) 264 SB
225 1100 1692 (     where n is the number of pages to be displayed.  If you do not specify n, ED types) 1692 SB
225 1159 1706 (     the 23 lines following the CP and then moves the CP forward 23 lines.  This leaves) 1706 SB
225 1218 1080 (     the CP pointing to the first character on the screen.) 1080 SB
225 1336 1772 (       To display the current page without moving the CP, enter OP.  The special character) 1772 SB
225 1396 1740 (     0 prevents the movement of the CP.  If you specify a negative number for n, P pages) 1740 SB
225 1455 818 (     backwards towards the top of the file.) 818 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c370 font
225 1573 776 (     The n: \(Line Number\) Command) 776 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
225 1691 1691 (       When line numbers are being displayed, ED accepts a line number as a command) 1691 SB
225 1751 1737 (        to specify a destination for the CP.  The line number command takes the following) 1737 SB
225 1810 213 (        form:) 213 SB
225 1928 155 (         n:) 155 SB
225 2046 1681 (     where n is the number of the destination line.  This command places the CP at the) 1681 SB
225 2106 1703 (     beginning of the specified line.  For example, the command 4: moves the CP to the) 1703 SB
225 2165 616 (     beginning of the fourth line.) 616 SB
225 2283 1706 (       Remember that ED dynamically renumbers text lines in the buffer each time a line) 1706 SB
225 2342 1716 (     is added or deleted.  Therefore, the number of the destination line you have in mind) 1716 SB
225 2401 587 (     can change during editing.) 587 SB
