225 1986 1509 (         The F command performs the simplest find function; it takes the form:) 1509 SB
225 2105 294 (           nfstring) 294 SB
225 2223 1744 (       where n is the occurrence of the string to be found.  Any number you enter must be) 1744 SB
225 2282 1770 (       positive because ED can only search from the CP to the bottom of the buffer.  If you) 1770 SB
225 2341 1782 (       enter no number, ED finds the next occurrence of the string in the file.  In the follow-) 1782 SB
225 2400 1351 (       ing example, the second occurrence of the word living is found.) 1351 SB
225 2519 317 (       1: *2fliving) 317 SB
225 2578 168 (       3: *) 168 SB
