225 1454 434 (     The N Command) 434 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
225 1572 1722 (       The N command extends the search function beyond the memory buffer to include) 1722 SB
225 1631 1730 (     the source file.  If the search is successful, it leaves the CP pointing to the first char-) 1730 SB
225 1690 1288 (     acter after the search string.  The N command takes the form:) 1288 SB
225 1809 289 (         nNstring) 289 SB
225 1927 1660 (     where n is the occurrence of the string to be found.  If no number is entered, ED) 1660 SB
225 1986 1695 (     looks for the next occurrence of the string in the file.  The case of the N command) 1695 SB
225 2045 1739 (     has the same effect on an N command as it does on an F command.  Note that if you) 1739 SB
225 2105 1662 (     follow an N command with another ED command, you must terminate the string) 1662 SB
225 2164 387 (     with a CTRL-Z.) 387 SB
