225 152 1766 (         When an N command is executed, ED searches the memory buffer for the specified) 1766 SB
225 211 1776 (       string, but if ED does not find the string, it does not issue an error message.  Instead,) 1776 SB
225 270 1713 (       ED automatically writes the searched data from the buffer into the new file.  Then) 1713 SB
225 330 1755 (       ED performs a OA command to fill the buffer with unsearched data from the source) 1755 SB
225 389 1761 (       file.  ED continues to search the buffer, write out data,, and append new data until it) 1761 SB
225 448 1755 (       either finds the string or reaches the end of the source file.  If ED reaches the end of) 1755 SB
225 507 1060 (       the source file, ED issues the following message:) 1060 SB
225 625 415 (       BREAK "*" AT) 415 SB
225 744 1735 (         Because ED writes the searched data to the new file before looking for more data) 1735 SB
225 803 1746 (       in the source file, ED usually writes the contents of the buffer to the new file before) 1746 SB
225 862 1343 (       finding the end of the source file and issuing the error message.) 1343 SB
225 980 1739 (       No,e: you must use the H command to continue an edit session after the source file) 1739 SB
225 1040 1025 (       is exhausted and the memory buffer is emptied.) 1025 SB
