32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
225 685 741 (      The X command takes the forms:) 741 SB
225 803 177 (         nX) 177 SB
225 862 379 (         nXfilespec^Z) 379 SB
225 980 1653 (    where n is the number of lines from the CP towards the bottom of the buffer that) 1653 SB
225 1040 1698 (    are to be transferred to a file.  Therefore, n must always be a positive number.  The) 1698 SB
225 1099 1693 (    nX command with no file specified creates a temporary file named X$$$$$$$.LIB.) 1693 SB
225 1158 1720 (    This file is erased when you terminate the edit session.  The nX command with a file) 1720 SB
225 1217 1802 (     specified creates a file of the specified name.  If no filetype is specified, LIB is assumed.) 1802 SB
225 1276 1697 (    This file is saved when you terminate the edit session.  If the X command is not the) 1697 SB
225 1335 1687 (    last command on the line, the command must be terminated by a CTRL-Z or ESC.) 1687 SB
225 1395 1515 (    In the following example, just one line is transferred to the temporary file:) 1515 SB
225 1513 190 (    1    *X) 190 SB
