225 152 1630 (      To execute an H command, ED first finalizes the new file, transferring all lines) 1630 SB
225 211 1704 (    remaining 'in the buffer and the source file to the new file.  Then ED closes the new) 1704 SB
225 270 1743 (    file, erases any BAK file that has the same file specification as the original source file,) 1743 SB
225 330 1672 (    and renames the original source file filename.BAK. ED then renames the new file,) 1672 SB
225 389 1731 (    which has had the filetype $$$, with the original file specification.  Finally, ED opens) 1731 SB
225 448 1672 (    the newly renamed file as the new source file for a new edit, and opens a new $$$) 1672 SB
225 507 1727 (    file.  When ED returns the * prompt, the CP is at the beginning of an empty memory) 1727 SB
225 566 183 (    buffer.) 183 SB
