32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c363 font
225 270 1746 (          A Q command abandons changes made since the beginning of the ED session and) 1746 SB
225 330 972 (         exits ED.  The Q command takes the form:) 972 SB
225 448 192 (            Q) 192 SB
225 566 704 (         followed by a carriage return.) 704 SB
225 685 1750 (          When you enter a Q command, ED verifies that you want to abandon the changes) 1750 SB
225 744 304 (         by asking) 304 SB
225 862 307 (         Q \(Y/N\)?) 307 SB
225 980 1755 (          You must respond with either a Y or an N; if you press any other key, ED repeats) 1755 SB
225 1040 1806 (         the question.  When you enter Y, ED erases the temporary file, closes the source file,) 1806 SB
225 1099 732 (         and returns control to CP/M 3.) 732 SB
225 1217 1751 (         Note: you can enter a CTRL-Break or a CTRL-C to return control immediately to) 1751 SB
225 1276 1689 (         CP/M 3. This does not give ED a chance to close the source or new files, but it) 1689 SB
225 1335 1048 (         prevents ED from deleting any temporary files.) 1048 SB
