225 1130 1614 (                            mand line to CP/M 3. Moves the cursor to the beginning of the) 1614 SB
225 1189 1266 (                            next line without erasing your previous input.) 1266 SB
225 1308 1537 (          CTRL-H    Deletes a character and moves the cursor left one character) 1537 SB
225 1367 536 (                            position.) 536 SB
225 1485 1613 (          CTRL-I      Moves the cursor to the next tab stop. Tab stops are automati-) 1613 SB
225 1544 1628 (                            cally set at each eighth column.  Has the same effect as pressing) 1628 SB
225 1604 633 (                            the TAB key.) 633 SB
225 1722 1566 (          CTRL-J     Sends the command line to CP/M 3 and returns the cursor to) 1566 SB
225 1781 1584 (                           the left of the current line.  Has the same effect as a RETURN) 1584 SB
225 1840 656 (                            or a CTRL-M.) 656 SB
225 1959 1565 (          CTRL-M   Sends the command line to CP/M 3 and returns the cursor to) 1565 SB
225 2018 1584 (                           the left of the current line.  Has the same effect as a RETURN) 1584 SB
225 2077 631 (                            or a CTRL-J.) 631 SB
225 2195 1643 (          CTRL-P     Echoes all console activity to the printer. The first time you type) 1643 SB
225 2254 1551 (                            CTRL-P, CP/M 3 rings a bell at your console.  You can use) 1551 SB
225 2314 1662 (                            CTRL-P after you halt scrolling with CTRL-S.  A second CTRL-) 1662 SB
225 2373 1636 (                            P ends printer echo; no bell rings.  CTRL-P has no effect if your) 1636 SB
225 2432 1030 (                            system does not include a printer.) 1030 SB
